//============================================================================
// nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads --- Calibre ANTENNA wrapper deck   (PROJECT-OWNED)
//
// Run it with:   DRC_GDS=/abs/path.gds scripts/calibre/run_ant.sh
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
// --------------------
// Same reason as the DRC wrapper beside it: the foundry antenna deck ships
// placeholder specification statements the customer is expected to replace --
// the layout path, the primary cell, and the results-database and
// summary-report filenames -- and they are literal strings, not variables. The
// deck's own text is not reproduced here: this repository is public and TSMC's
// licence does not permit it. Read the block in your own PDK.
//
// `DRC ICSTATION YES` is what makes overriding them from a top-level wrapper
// legal; see the long note in nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads.drc.rules. Verified on
// Calibre v2023.1_18.8.
//
// WHICH FOUNDRY DECK: this file does not name one. $ANT_FOUNDRY_DECK is resolved
// per site from $(TSMC_65_HOME) by ASIC/genus-innovus/drc_project.mk, which is
// gitignored. It must be the antenna deck for the SAME metal stack as the DRC
// deck and as the Innovus GdsOutMap used by write_stream. The deck's release
// name encodes a metal stack and a purchased revision, so it is site
// configuration, not source. See ci/site.env.example.
//
// WHY IT MATTERS
// --------------
// Innovus check_process_antenna reports "No Violations Found" on this design,
// and it is backed by real data (the std-cell LEF carries thousands of antenna
// gate-area/diff-area entries). But that is the ROUTER's model over a stream
// with no transistors in it. The foundry deck has never been run here -- there
// is no .ant.summary anywhere in this repo -- and the Europractice mini@sic
// manual is unambiguous that antenna violations are not acceptable in a
// submission.
//
// READ THE RESULT WITH THE BLACK-BOX CAVEAT IN MIND. Standard cells, IO and
// bond pads stream as empty references (their layouts are imported by the
// broker), so every gate-area term inside a cell is absent. Checks that need
// gate area will under-report. The signal here is the ROUTING contribution:
// long antennas on nets that reach a cell pin.
//
// The foundry deck is READ-ONLY (the PDK mount is shared lab collateral) and is
// not copied, patched or sed-ed by this flow.
//============================================================================

// ---- must come first: enables top-level override of the deck's placeholders
DRC ICSTATION YES

// ---- input layout -----------------------------------------------------------
// $DRC_GDS is expanded by Calibre itself in file-path strings. LAYOUT PRIMARY
// must stay literal -- SVRF does not expand env vars in cell names.
LAYOUT PATH    "$DRC_GDS"
LAYOUT SYSTEM  GDSII
LAYOUT PRIMARY "nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads"

// ---- outputs (relative -> they land in the run directory) --------------------
DRC RESULTS DATABASE "nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads.ant.results" ASCII
DRC SUMMARY REPORT   "nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads.ant.summary" REPLACE HIER
DRC CELL NAME YES CELL SPACE XFORM

DRC MAXIMUM RESULTS 1000
DRC MAXIMUM VERTEX  4096

// ---- process option ---------------------------------------------------------
// We are CLN65LP (tcbn65lp std cells, tphn65lpgv2od3_sl IO). The shipped decks
// leave LP undefined; define it here, before the INCLUDE, so the LP-specific
// rule variants are selected. Harmless if this deck ignores it.
#DEFINE LP

// ---- the foundry antenna deck, unmodified -----------------------------------
// Resolved per site, never named here. run_drc.sh expands and readability-checks
// this before launching, so a missing or wrong value is a sentence rather than an
// SVRF error deep in the deck.
INCLUDE "$ANT_FOUNDRY_DECK"
